    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0107_99713ee443cc.png\" style=\"width: 360px; height: 167px;\" /></p><p>Current will flow from the diode when diode is in forward biased.<br />Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mi>V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi></math> will be &#39;zero&#39;, when diode is reverse biased.<img src=\"assets\\st0107_1d29349d75d5.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 156px;\" /></p>"
